{
  "format": "call-of-slop-construct-part/1",
  "name": "Saw Block",
  "description": "Weld it on a Sawmill Core's +x side, or beside another Saw Block: the Core splits its blocks into squares, each one band mill whose carriage strokes a log through the band, and every square saws at once; a bigger square takes a bigger log. Each block of an n x n square adds 1 + n/4 to the Core's rate (a lone block 1.25, a 3 x 3's 1.75 each), so bigger squares pay more. A wrecked block keeps its square and adds nothing until mended. No power of its own: the Core draws a share for it. The bands and carriages cut: keep clear while it works.",
